<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15786" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτύνω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ]</span>, fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῠνῶ,</span>
		
			Ion.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῠνέω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.277
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤρτῡνα,</span>
			
				Med.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-υνάμην,</span>
			
				Pass.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ύνθην</span>:— 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτύω</span>
			, chiefly used in 
				Ep.
			 (in later Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γηράσκουσα ἡ ἐπιστήμη σοφίαν ἀρτύνει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					1.25.11
				</span></i>
			), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεύδεά τ᾽ ἀρτύνοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.366
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόχον ἀρτύναντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.469
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μνηστῆρσιν θάνατον κακὸν ἀρτύναντε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.153
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑσμίνην ἤρτυνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.303
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτύνθη δὲ μάχη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.216
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτυνέουσιν ἔεδνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.277
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυργηδὸν σφέας αὐτοὺς</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτύναντες</span>
			<i>putting</i> themselves <i>in order, dressing</i> their ranks,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.43
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				86
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				13.152
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυκινὴν ἠρτύνετο βουλήν</span>
			<i>prepared his</i> counsel, <i><span class="en">
				2.55
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρτύναντο ἐρετμὰ τροποῖς ἐν
				δερματίνοισι</span>
			<i>fitted</i> them with . . , <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.782
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.53
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
